1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,940
Mugi, are you ready?

2
00:00:08,700 --> 00:00:09,940
Wait, hold on a sec.

3
00:00:10,740 --> 00:00:12,100
I'm the assistant today.

4
00:00:13,240 --> 00:00:15,120
Are you stupid or something, Mugi?

5
00:00:15,320 --> 00:00:16,540
I'll take care of that for you.

6
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:18,280
Now go on, get out of here.

7
00:00:18,700 --> 00:00:20,120
You two go get some crepes together.

8
00:00:23,620 --> 00:00:24,140
Sanai.

9
00:00:25,780 --> 00:00:27,400
You heading home now, Hanabi?

10
00:00:27,960 --> 00:00:28,260
Yeah.

11
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:29,420
Yeah?

12
00:00:30,140 --> 00:00:32,040
Would you mind walking home together?

13
00:00:32,680 --> 00:00:35,960
We haven't really been able to hang out that much with each other this year.

14
00:00:36,340 --> 00:00:37,200
Thanks for waiting.

15
00:00:37,680 --> 00:00:39,000
Yeah, well, um...

16
00:00:40,020 --> 00:00:41,420
Oh, that's right.

17
00:00:41,460 --> 00:00:43,220
You've been walking home with Mugi lately.

18
00:00:43,440 --> 00:00:44,140
I'm sorry.

19
00:00:44,920 --> 00:00:45,980
No, it's fine.

20
00:00:47,420 --> 00:00:48,960
He is your boyfriend, after all.

21
00:00:49,960 --> 00:00:51,240
He comes first.

22
00:00:53,700 --> 00:00:54,780
Next time, okay?

23
00:00:54,780 --> 00:01:00,120
Man, he's so lucky.

24
00:01:00,520 --> 00:01:02,700
Well, he is pretty popular with the ladies.

25
00:01:03,320 --> 00:01:05,360
You know, they make a good couple.

26
00:01:05,360 --> 00:01:12,060
Are you sure you didn't want to walk with your friend?

27
00:01:12,060 --> 00:01:13,560
I'm good.

28
00:01:13,560 --> 00:01:14,860
Give me some of that.

29
00:01:25,400 --> 00:01:28,100
You stop that right now!

30
00:01:28,100 --> 00:01:34,220
You scared me.

31
00:01:36,340 --> 00:01:36,980
What?

32
00:01:37,520 --> 00:01:39,940
Who exactly are you?

33
00:01:39,940 --> 00:01:47,120
You?

34
00:01:48,120 --> 00:01:49,880
You're right.

35
00:01:49,880 --> 00:01:51,300
You're right.

36
00:03:14,927 --> 00:03:18,927
Mugi and I are childhood friends from the same apartment building.

37
00:03:19,927 --> 00:03:21,927
Aw, aren't you cute?

38
00:03:21,927 --> 00:03:26,927
Did you know that you and Mugi look like the perfect image of a prince and princess when you're together?

39
00:03:27,927 --> 00:03:31,927
A prince and princess? How romantic.

40
00:03:32,927 --> 00:03:36,927
As a young girl, the thought of that captured my imagination.

41
00:03:37,927 --> 00:03:39,927
I'm a princess.

42
00:03:39,927 --> 00:03:43,927
I spent a whole year growing out my hair.

43
00:03:43,927 --> 00:03:46,927
I stopped playing with all the smelly boys.

44
00:03:46,927 --> 00:03:49,927
And I spent my time collecting only cute things.

45
00:03:49,927 --> 00:03:53,927
I tried my hardest to become a princess worthy of a real prince.

46
00:03:53,927 --> 00:03:57,927
So then, all that was left was for a prince to notice me.

47
00:03:57,927 --> 00:03:59,927
And then my dream would come true.

48
00:04:02,927 --> 00:04:04,927
Yeah, so, um...

49
00:04:04,927 --> 00:04:07,927
This is Noriko Kamomebata.

50
00:04:07,927 --> 00:04:08,927
Mocha!

51
00:04:08,927 --> 00:04:11,927
She's my childhood friend.

52
00:04:11,927 --> 00:04:14,927
This is Hanabi Yasuraoka, my girlfriend.

53
00:04:15,927 --> 00:04:16,927
I'm not lying.

54
00:04:17,927 --> 00:04:18,927
That can't be!

55
00:04:18,927 --> 00:04:21,927
Uh, I remember you from grade school.

56
00:04:23,927 --> 00:04:25,927
Huh? You know her?

57
00:04:25,927 --> 00:04:26,927
Let me see...

58
00:04:26,927 --> 00:04:28,927
Kamomekamokamo, that's it?

59
00:04:28,927 --> 00:04:29,927
That's too many Kamos!

60
00:04:29,927 --> 00:04:30,927
Then, Noriko.

61
00:04:30,927 --> 00:04:33,927
Of course that's what you would remember!

62
00:04:33,927 --> 00:04:35,927
It's Mocha Kamomebata!

63
00:04:35,927 --> 00:04:39,927
For the record, Mocha is short for meeting the most cutest angel, Mocha!

64
00:04:39,927 --> 00:04:41,927
I won't answer to anything else!

65
00:04:42,927 --> 00:04:43,927
Yeah, yeah.

66
00:04:43,927 --> 00:04:46,927
As I recall, you've always been a pain in the butt, now haven't you?

67
00:04:46,927 --> 00:04:51,927
And as I remember correctly, you were always an awful, ungrateful person!

68
00:04:51,927 --> 00:04:54,927
Why is someone like you dating Moogie anyway?

69
00:04:54,927 --> 00:04:57,927
Poor Moogie getting tricked by a girl like this!

70
00:04:57,927 --> 00:05:00,927
You just pretend to be nice in front of him, don't you?

71
00:05:00,927 --> 00:05:01,927
Not at all.

72
00:05:01,927 --> 00:05:03,927
Wow, I'm impressed you noticed.

73
00:05:03,927 --> 00:05:04,927
You're right.

74
00:05:04,927 --> 00:05:06,927
She can be horrible.

75
00:05:06,927 --> 00:05:07,927
Sometimes.

76
00:05:07,927 --> 00:05:09,927
You're one to talk, Moogie.

77
00:05:10,927 --> 00:05:12,927
What are you saying?

78
00:05:12,927 --> 00:05:14,927
Is that what you like?

79
00:05:15,927 --> 00:05:18,927
Well, it's just a part that makes her Hanabi after all.

80
00:05:22,927 --> 00:05:23,927
Thanks.

81
00:05:23,927 --> 00:05:25,927
I like everything about you too, Moogie.

82
00:05:30,927 --> 00:05:31,927
Listen up, kid.

83
00:05:31,927 --> 00:05:33,927
I wouldn't go around clinging on to things...

84
00:05:34,927 --> 00:05:36,927
...that aren't yours.

85
00:05:37,927 --> 00:05:42,927
So, you know...

86
00:05:43,927 --> 00:05:44,927
Yesterday...

87
00:05:44,927 --> 00:05:46,927
Did you have to be so harsh to her?

88
00:05:48,927 --> 00:05:49,927
What do you mean by that?

89
00:05:49,927 --> 00:05:51,927
She likes you, doesn't she?

90
00:05:51,927 --> 00:05:52,927
Yeah?

91
00:05:52,927 --> 00:05:53,927
So what?

92
00:05:54,927 --> 00:05:55,927
Well, that's just it.

93
00:05:55,927 --> 00:05:58,927
Actually, why don't you turn her down properly?

94
00:05:59,927 --> 00:06:02,927
I didn't notice you looking at her in that lustful way that you have.

95
00:06:03,927 --> 00:06:05,927
It's the nice thing to do, after all.

96
00:06:06,927 --> 00:06:07,927
Well...

97
00:06:07,927 --> 00:06:09,927
Look, I understand a part of you cares about her.

98
00:06:11,927 --> 00:06:12,927
Ow!

99
00:06:14,927 --> 00:06:15,927
Come on.

100
00:06:15,927 --> 00:06:17,927
You're just clinging to your superiority.

101
00:06:17,927 --> 00:06:20,927
Why does it bother you?

102
00:06:21,927 --> 00:06:22,927
Hm?

103
00:06:22,927 --> 00:06:24,927
Is it because you want me all to yourself?

104
00:06:25,927 --> 00:06:26,927
You're jealous?

105
00:06:26,927 --> 00:06:27,927
Don't be such an idiot.

106
00:06:29,927 --> 00:06:30,927
Look, I'm just possessive.

107
00:06:31,927 --> 00:06:32,927
That's all.

108
00:06:34,927 --> 00:06:35,927
I don't know.

109
00:06:37,927 --> 00:06:38,927
Is that really it?

110
00:06:38,927 --> 00:06:39,927
Who knows?

111
00:06:39,927 --> 00:06:54,927
I have to fight for my life every day on this thing.

112
00:06:55,927 --> 00:06:57,927
There's something wrong with Japan's commuter rush.

113
00:06:57,927 --> 00:07:03,927
I want to see Mugi and his handsome face.

114
00:07:06,927 --> 00:07:08,927
I hate wasting my time always thinking about him.

115
00:07:09,927 --> 00:07:11,927
It's unbecoming of a princess.

116
00:07:12,927 --> 00:07:15,927
Plus, it hurts so much thinking about him like that.

117
00:07:20,927 --> 00:07:23,927
I just end up recreating him in my mind to fit my needs.

118
00:07:23,927 --> 00:07:24,927
Scary.

119
00:07:31,927 --> 00:07:32,927
Oh.

120
00:07:33,927 --> 00:07:34,927
You getting some bread too?

121
00:07:36,927 --> 00:07:37,927
Um, yeah.

122
00:07:38,927 --> 00:07:39,927
Here.

123
00:07:39,927 --> 00:07:40,927
A sweet and savory one.

124
00:07:41,927 --> 00:07:42,927
He got the ones I wanted without asking.

125
00:07:43,927 --> 00:07:44,927
Mugi!

126
00:07:44,927 --> 00:07:45,927
I love you!

127
00:07:45,927 --> 00:07:46,927
I can't breathe!

128
00:07:46,927 --> 00:07:47,927
Let go of me, Mocha!

129
00:07:48,927 --> 00:07:49,927
Oh, Mugi!

130
00:07:49,927 --> 00:07:51,927
The time I get to be with him is the best!

131
00:07:52,927 --> 00:07:54,927
That's exactly what I live for.

132
00:07:57,927 --> 00:07:58,927
Huh?

133
00:07:59,927 --> 00:08:00,927
I'm so jealous of your lunch.

134
00:08:01,927 --> 00:08:02,927
I've got fried chicken.

135
00:08:02,927 --> 00:08:03,927
You want some?

136
00:08:03,927 --> 00:08:04,927
Yeah.

137
00:08:05,927 --> 00:08:06,927
Say, ah!

138
00:08:07,927 --> 00:08:08,927
Ah!

139
00:08:11,927 --> 00:08:12,927
The fried chicken disappeared.

140
00:08:13,927 --> 00:08:14,927
Oh, I think you're right.

141
00:08:14,927 --> 00:08:15,927
You think it's poltergeists?

142
00:08:16,927 --> 00:08:17,927
Hey!

143
00:08:17,927 --> 00:08:18,927
Don't ignore me!

144
00:08:19,927 --> 00:08:20,927
Cut it out, it hurts!

145
00:08:21,927 --> 00:08:22,927
You're the little brat that needs to cut it out.

146
00:08:23,927 --> 00:08:25,927
What the hell are you doing tagging along during our lunch date

147
00:08:26,927 --> 00:08:27,927
and being so damn annoying?

148
00:08:28,927 --> 00:08:30,927
Didn't I warn you before about this?

149
00:08:31,927 --> 00:08:32,927
You... just shut out!

150
00:08:33,927 --> 00:08:34,927
Is she an animal?

151
00:08:34,927 --> 00:08:35,927
Evil succubus!

152
00:08:36,927 --> 00:08:38,927
I bet you don't even like Mugi that much anyway!

153
00:08:39,927 --> 00:08:40,927
She's just using you, Mugi!

154
00:08:41,927 --> 00:08:44,927
She wants to brag that she's with you because you're so cool and popular in school!

155
00:08:45,927 --> 00:08:46,927
I know that's all she cares about!

156
00:08:47,927 --> 00:08:48,927
Yeah, whatever.

157
00:08:49,927 --> 00:08:50,927
I see. You're very observant.

158
00:08:51,927 --> 00:08:53,927
Stop acting like this is all okay with you, Mugi!

159
00:08:54,927 --> 00:08:55,927
Fine, but mark my words!

160
00:08:56,927 --> 00:08:57,927
I'm never giving up!

161
00:08:58,927 --> 00:08:59,927
Excuse me!

162
00:08:59,927 --> 00:09:00,927
Oh, she ran away.

163
00:09:01,927 --> 00:09:02,927
Don't run away if you're not gonna give up.

164
00:09:02,927 --> 00:09:04,927
Well, she's just frightened of you.

165
00:09:05,927 --> 00:09:06,927
She was even polite.

166
00:09:06,927 --> 00:09:07,927
She's so irritating!

167
00:09:08,927 --> 00:09:09,927
Just the worst!

168
00:09:11,927 --> 00:09:12,927
Using?

169
00:09:17,927 --> 00:09:18,927
Hey! Stop!

170
00:09:19,927 --> 00:09:20,927
Don't run in the hallway!

171
00:09:21,927 --> 00:09:22,927
Okay!

172
00:09:22,927 --> 00:09:26,927
I've always wanted to say that.

173
00:09:27,927 --> 00:09:29,927
Just like on TV when the kids are running in the hall.

174
00:09:30,927 --> 00:09:31,927
Good for you.

175
00:09:32,927 --> 00:09:34,927
Anyway, why is it that I have to help you with this again?

176
00:09:35,927 --> 00:09:36,927
Uh...

177
00:09:37,927 --> 00:09:39,927
Because it's hard to ask anybody besides you.

178
00:09:40,927 --> 00:09:41,927
What am I ever going to do with you?

179
00:09:43,927 --> 00:09:45,927
So, where are we taking these papers?

180
00:09:45,927 --> 00:09:47,927
Over to the language prep room.

181
00:09:48,927 --> 00:09:49,927
Uh...

182
00:09:49,927 --> 00:09:50,927
Doesn't that mean...

183
00:09:53,927 --> 00:09:54,927
We're all alone!

184
00:09:55,927 --> 00:09:56,927
This is it.

185
00:09:56,927 --> 00:09:57,927
I can't ruin it and be nervous.

186
00:09:58,927 --> 00:09:59,927
Leave the handouts there.

187
00:09:59,927 --> 00:10:00,927
What I need to do here is...

188
00:10:02,927 --> 00:10:03,927
That was heavy.

189
00:10:04,927 --> 00:10:05,927
I need Brother to look at me.

190
00:10:05,927 --> 00:10:07,927
I need to make him see me as a woman.

191
00:10:08,927 --> 00:10:09,927
Even just a little.

192
00:10:11,927 --> 00:10:12,927
Uh...

193
00:10:23,927 --> 00:10:24,927
A piano?

194
00:10:32,927 --> 00:10:33,927
That must be her.

195
00:10:34,927 --> 00:10:35,927
Isn't she great?

196
00:10:36,927 --> 00:10:37,927
I can always hear it.

197
00:10:46,927 --> 00:10:50,927
Obviously a stupid music teacher is going to know how to play the piano!

198
00:10:51,927 --> 00:10:52,927
Don't say that into the mic!

199
00:10:52,927 --> 00:10:53,927
Get into the mic!

200
00:11:04,927 --> 00:11:06,927
You ever consider giving up?

201
00:11:06,927 --> 00:11:07,927
You've got two.

202
00:11:09,927 --> 00:11:10,927
Listen, Hanabi.

203
00:11:11,927 --> 00:11:13,927
There's plenty of other hot guys around here.

204
00:11:14,927 --> 00:11:15,927
Uh...

205
00:11:15,927 --> 00:11:16,927
Don't worry.

206
00:11:16,927 --> 00:11:18,927
I don't mean me or anything like that.

207
00:11:20,927 --> 00:11:21,927
You have to sing too!

208
00:11:22,927 --> 00:11:23,927
What?

209
00:11:23,927 --> 00:11:37,927
Brother's very...

210
00:11:40,927 --> 00:11:41,927
Brother is here...

211
00:11:42,927 --> 00:11:45,927
Brother is cool, you got that?!

212
00:11:45,927 --> 00:11:46,927
Oh, you got that?

213
00:11:49,447 --> 00:11:50,247
Don't cry.

214
00:11:55,667 --> 00:11:57,707
You get it, don't you?

215
00:11:58,407 --> 00:12:00,127
You're in the same situation.

216
00:12:01,187 --> 00:12:04,327
You know that it's not a matter of deciding to just give them up or not.

217
00:12:05,407 --> 00:12:08,807
Once you've fallen, you can't think of anyone else but them.

218
00:12:09,867 --> 00:12:10,287
I know.

219
00:12:14,447 --> 00:12:15,427
I get it.

220
00:12:15,927 --> 00:12:17,987
Why did I end up having to fall for them?

221
00:12:19,687 --> 00:12:23,307
But it doesn't always feel painful.

222
00:12:25,307 --> 00:12:32,227
That's why I can't bring myself to wish that we'd never met.

223
00:12:34,127 --> 00:12:35,927
That would...

224
00:12:36,567 --> 00:12:38,527
How do I say?

225
00:12:39,527 --> 00:12:40,947
Make it even worse to bear.

226
00:12:40,947 --> 00:12:41,287
I'm sorry.

227
00:12:45,827 --> 00:12:46,387
What?

228
00:12:46,647 --> 00:12:47,427
What now?

229
00:12:49,687 --> 00:12:50,787
Stick out your tongue.

230
00:12:50,787 --> 00:12:57,167
Mugi.

231
00:12:57,167 --> 00:12:58,167
Mugi.

232
00:12:58,167 --> 00:12:59,167
Mugi?

233
00:12:59,167 --> 00:13:05,167
Mugi, touch me.

234
00:13:05,167 --> 00:13:12,167
Wait, hey, Mugi.

235
00:13:12,167 --> 00:13:19,167
Don't you mean... brother?

236
00:13:19,167 --> 00:13:22,167
You're right.

237
00:13:22,167 --> 00:13:28,167
Mugi...

238
00:13:28,167 --> 00:13:33,167
Don't you mean... brother?

239
00:13:33,167 --> 00:13:37,167
You're right.

240
00:13:45,167 --> 00:13:51,167
Mugi...

241
00:13:51,167 --> 00:13:54,167
I didn't think I'd think of that with you.

242
00:13:54,167 --> 00:13:58,167
What's more, that I'd be relieved.

243
00:14:02,167 --> 00:14:04,167
I think...

244
00:14:04,167 --> 00:14:07,167
I'd rather she yelled at me.

245
00:14:07,167 --> 00:14:18,167
Evil Succubus!

246
00:14:18,167 --> 00:14:21,167
I bet you don't even like Mugi that much anyway!

247
00:14:21,167 --> 00:14:24,167
She's just using you, Mugi!

248
00:14:24,167 --> 00:14:27,167
Using?

249
00:14:34,167 --> 00:14:37,167
What if... the one being used...

250
00:14:37,167 --> 00:14:39,167
is actually her?

251
00:14:42,167 --> 00:14:45,167
Ah! Sanai! Good morning!

252
00:14:45,167 --> 00:14:48,167
Hey! What's wrong, Hanabi?

253
00:14:48,167 --> 00:14:50,167
Your face is bright red!

254
00:14:50,167 --> 00:14:52,167
I slept in late.

255
00:14:52,167 --> 00:14:55,167
Turns out I had plenty of time, huh?

256
00:14:55,167 --> 00:14:56,167
Looks like it.

257
00:14:56,167 --> 00:15:11,167
You... want to talk about romance?

258
00:15:14,167 --> 00:15:17,167
Huh? Seems harmless to me. You should go do it.

259
00:15:17,167 --> 00:15:21,167
Hmm... what am I supposed to talk about?

260
00:15:21,167 --> 00:15:24,167
Poor thing. You don't have a lot of female friends.

261
00:15:25,167 --> 00:15:26,167
I do too.

262
00:15:26,167 --> 00:15:27,167
Yeah?

263
00:15:28,167 --> 00:15:30,167
I'm being serious!

264
00:15:30,167 --> 00:15:31,167
Like who, then?

265
00:15:32,167 --> 00:15:35,167
Like... Sanai. So there.

266
00:15:35,167 --> 00:15:36,167
Is that it?

267
00:15:36,167 --> 00:15:37,167
Is that it?

268
00:15:38,167 --> 00:15:41,167
Hanabi! That's why you should go meet with them.

